10: # Implementation Flow (All Languages)
11: 
12: See `COMMON_RULES.md` for rules that apply to all languages.
13: 
14: Unlike the per-language `*_RULES.md` files, these rules are **language-independent** and
15: **always apply**. They are not subject to the "some rules may not apply to this project"
16: filtering — include them in every project's `CODING_RULES.md`.
17: 
18: These rules define the end-to-end workflow an AI agent must follow when planning and
19: implementing changes. Each step is an existing skill referenced by its slash name; run the
20: skill rather than reimplementing its behavior.
21: 
22: ---
23: 
24: ## Delegation backends (Codex / DeepSeek)
25: 
26: Some of the workflow steps below can be delegated to an external CLI instead
27: of being performed by the agent itself. Two backends are supported, and they
28: are **mutually exclusive** — at most one is enabled at a time:
29: 
30: - `<!-- codex: enabled -->` — delegate to Codex
31: - `<!-- deepseek: enabled -->` — delegate to DeepSeek
32: - Neither marker `enabled` (or no marker) — do NOT delegate; perform the same
33:   checks yourself via the listed fallback skills.
34: 
35: Never call the backend CLI directly. Both backends are invoked through one
36: wrapper script installed in the project by `/coding-rules:codex on` /
37: `/coding-rules:deepseek on`, from the repo root:
38: 
39: ```
40: tools/coding_rules_delegate.sh <backend> <prompt-file> <log-file>
41: ```
42: 
43: `<backend>` is `codex` or `deepseek`. The wrapper holds the backend flags, the
44: log redirection and the closed stdin — the agent never types them. That keeps
45: the command line short and boring, which is what stops Claude Code's permission
46: classifier from denying the call.
47: 
48: Use the Bash tool with the `.sh`. Only if the Bash tool is unavailable, use the
49: PowerShell tool with `tools/coding_rules_delegate.ps1` (same three arguments).
50: Type the command exactly as written above — the permission entry matches a
51: literal command prefix, so an absolute path or an extra `cmd` wrapper misses it.
52: 
53: Read precedence if both markers somehow end up `enabled`: Codex wins, then
54: DeepSeek, then the self-fallback.
55: 
56: **Self-fallback in a subagent.** When neither backend is enabled, prefer
57: running each fallback skill in a subagent (Agent/Task tool, `general-purpose`
58: type) rather than inline — the skill's file reads and reasoning stay out of
59: the main context window. The subagent runs the skill and returns **only**
60: its summary (and the list of files it changed). Any file edits the skill
61: makes (plan file, code) persist, so the main agent picks them up.
62: 
63: Exceptions that MUST stay in the main context: `/plan:dry-checked` (it
64: reloads the adjusted plan INTO context) and restating the
65: Definition-of-Done / DRY gate aloud.
66: 
67: **Graphify preamble (optional).** If this project's `CODING_RULES.md` includes
68: the graphify addon, prepend its graphify delegate preamble to every `<PROMPT>`
69: below before invoking the backend CLI (see the graphify addon's "Delegated
70: checks" section). If the addon is not present, send `<PROMPT>` unchanged.
71: 
72: The markers are managed by `/coding-rules:codex on|off|status|test` and
73: `/coding-rules:deepseek on|off|status|test` (or set during
74: `/coding-rules:apply`). Do not flip them yourself without the user asking.
75: 
76: ### Delegation contract (never let a delegate hang)
77: 
78: Applies to EVERY delegated `<PROMPT>` below, both backends. A delegate that
79: stops to ask a question blocks forever on stdin nobody can answer — these four
80: rules make that impossible and leave a debug trail when it happens anyway.
--- tools/coding_rules_delegate.ps1
1: # Delegate one coding-rules check to an external CLI.
2: # usage: coding_rules_delegate.ps1 <codex|deepseek> <prompt-file> <log-file>
3: #
4: # The prompt lives in a file so no long text reaches the command line, and the
5: # backend flags / redirection stay in here. Installed by /coding-rules:codex on
6: # or /coding-rules:deepseek on -- do not edit in the project, it gets overwritten.
7: param(
8:     [Parameter(Mandatory = $true)][ValidateSet('codex', 'deepseek')][string]$Backend,
9:     [Parameter(Mandatory = $true)][string]$PromptFile,
10:     [Parameter(Mandatory = $true)][string]$LogFile
11: )
12: 
13: $ErrorActionPreference = 'Continue'
14: 
15: if (-not (Test-Path -LiteralPath $PromptFile -PathType Leaf)) {
16:     Write-Error "prompt file not found: $PromptFile"
17:     exit 2
